      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "studio-band",
      "description": "Sticky near-black app bar carrying the brand mark and nav.",
      "html": "<header class=\"ds-band\"><span class=\"ds-band-brand\"><svg width=\"26\" height=\"26\" viewBox=\"0 0 32 32\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"32\" height=\"32\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#17181b\"/><rect x=\"8\" y=\"6\" width=\"16\" height=\"20\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#fff\"/><rect x=\"10.5\" y=\"10\" width=\"11\" height=\"3.2\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#ffe14d\"/><rect x=\"11.5\" y=\"11\" width=\"9\" height=\"1.2\" fill=\"#17181b\"/><rect x=\"11.5\" y=\"16\" width=\"9\" height=\"1.4\" rx=\".7\" fill=\"#17181b\"/><rect x=\"11.5\" y=\"19.5\" width=\"6\" height=\"1.4\" rx=\".7\" fill=\"#17181b\"/></svg>AI Interviewer</span><nav><a class=\"ds-band-link\" href=\"#\">New interview</a><a class=\"ds-band-link\" href=\"#\">Save history</a></nav></header>",
      "css": ".ds-band{font-family:\"Atkinson Hyperlegible Next\",system-ui,sans-serif;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;height:60px;padding:0 24px;background:#17181b;color:#f4f5f7}.ds-band-brand{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;font-weight:800;font-size:1.0625rem;letter-spacing:-0.01em}.ds-band nav{display:flex;gap:4px}.ds-band-link{color:#f4f5f7;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.8125rem;font-weight:700;padding:4px 12px;border-radius:999px;transition:background-color 250ms}.ds-band-link:hover{background:rgba(255,255,255,0.08)}.ds-band-link:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #2f5bd3;outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Answer Field",
      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "input-field",
      "description": "Outlined paper field; border and label turn pencil on focus.",
      "html": "<label class=\"ds-field\"><span class=\"ds-speaker\">You</span><textarea class=\"ds-input\" rows=\"4\" placeholder=\"Answer as you would out loud.\"></textarea></label>",
      "css": ".ds-field{font-family:\"Atkinson Hyperlegible Next\",system-ui,sans-serif;display:block}.ds-speaker{display:block;font-size:0.75rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#17181b;margin-bottom:6px}.ds-input{font-family:\"Atkinson Hyperlegible Next\",system-ui,sans-serif;width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;background:#fff;color:#17181b;border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.23);border-radius:6px;padding:16.5px 14px;font-size:1.0625rem;line-height:1.7;resize:vertical}.ds-input:hover{border-color:#17181b}.ds-input:focus{outline:none;border:2px solid #2f5bd3;padding:15.5px 13px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Score Chip",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "chip",
      "description": "Score band: spike-tape outline, icon, and label together; never colour alone.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-chip\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path fill=\"#1f7a4d\" d=\"M12 2C6.48 2 2 6.48 2 12s4.48 10 10 10 10-4.48 10-10S17.52 2 12 2zM9.29 16.29 5.7 12.7a.996.996 0 1 1 1.41-1.41L10 14.17l6.88-6.88a.996.996 0 1 1 1.41 1.41l-7.59 7.59a.996.996 0 0 1-1.41 0z\"/></svg>8/10 · Strong</span>",
      "css": ".ds-chip{font-family:\"Atkinson Hyperlegible Next\",system-ui,sans-serif;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;height:24px;padding:0 8px 0 4px;border:1px solid #1f7a4d;border-radius:4px;background:#fff;color:#17181b;font-size:0.8125rem;font-weight:700}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Highlight Tag",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "highlight-tag",
      "description": "Ink on highlighter for a run in progress.",
      "html": "<a class=\"ds-tag\" href=\"#\">In progress · Resume</a>",
      "css": ".ds-tag{font-family:\"Atkinson Hyperlegible Next\",system-ui,sans-serif;display:inline-block;background:#ffe14d;color:#17181b;font-size:0.8125rem;font-weight:700;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:3px;text-decoration:none}.ds-tag:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #2f5bd3;outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Scene Rail",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "scene-current",
      "description": "Numbered scenes: done (check), current (highlighter sweep), upcoming (muted).",
      "html": "<ol class=\"ds-rail\"><li class=\"ds-scene\"><span class=\"ds-num\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-label=\"Answered\"><path fill=\"currentColor\" d=\"M9 16.17 5.53 12.7a.996.996 0 1 0-1.41 1.41l4.18 4.18c.39.39 1.02.39 1.41 0L20.29 7.71a.996.996 0 1 0-1.41-1.41z\"/></svg></span><span class=\"ds-q\">Walk me through a design de…</span></li><li class=\"ds-scene ds-current\" aria-current=\"step\"><span class=\"ds-num\">3</span><span class=\"ds-q\">Tell me about a time resear…</span></li><li class=\"ds-scene ds-upcoming\"><span class=\"ds-num\">4</span><span class=\"ds-q\">Not asked yet</span></li></ol>",
      "css": "@keyframes ds-sweep{from{background-size:0% 100%}to{background-size:100% 100%}}.ds-rail{font-family:\"Atkinson Hyperlegible Next\",system-ui,sans-serif;list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;width:240px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px}.ds-scene{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;min-height:36px;padding:6px 8px;border-radius:6px;font-size:0.875rem;color:#17181b}.ds-scene:hover{background:rgba(0,0,0,0.04)}.ds-num{width:22px;flex-shrink:0;font-weight:800;display:inline-flex;justify-content:center}.ds-q{overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap}.ds-upcoming{color:#55585f}.ds-current{background-image:linear-gradient(#ffe14d,#ffe14d);background-repeat:no-repeat;background-size:100% 100%;font-weight:700;animation:ds-sweep 420ms cubic-bezier(0.22,1,0.36,1)}.ds-current:hover{background-color:transparent}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-current{animation:none}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Script Row with Coach Notes",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "script-page",
      "description": "A script page: interviewer cue, your line, coach notes in pencil on a wash panel under the line.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-page\"><div class=\"ds-sp\">Interviewer · Question 1</div><div class=\"ds-cue\">Walk me through a design decision you would defend.</div><div class=\"ds-row\"><div><div class=\"ds-sp ds-you\">You</div><p class=\"ds-line\">At Starling I pushed back on a custom date picker the engineers wanted to build.</p></div><aside class=\"ds-notes\"><div class=\"ds-sp ds-coach\">Coach</div><p class=\"ds-note\">Strong, concrete example. Next time, say how you brought the lead round.</p></aside></div></article>",
      "css": ".ds-page{font-family:\"Atkinson Hyperlegible Next\",system-ui,sans-serif;background:#fff;border:1px solid #d9dbe0;border-radius:6px;padding:40px 48px;color:#17181b;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-sp{font-size:0.75rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#55585f;margin-bottom:6px}.ds-you{color:#17181b}.ds-coach{color:#2f5bd3}.ds-cue{font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:700;line-height:1.35;letter-spacing:-0.01em;max-width:36em;margin-bottom:24px}.ds-row{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;max-width:42em}.ds-line{margin:0;font-size:1.0625rem;line-height:1.7;max-width:40em}.ds-notes{background:#eef2fc;border-left:1px dashed #2f5bd3;border-radius:6px;padding:16px 20px}.ds-note{margin:0;font-size:0.9375rem;line-height:1.6;color:#2f5bd3}@media (max-width:899px){.ds-page{padding:24px 20px}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Audition Sides",
    "overview": "The interview is a rehearsal script you run. A near-black studio band holds the brand and navigation; script pages are bright white sheets (charcoal in dark mode) laid on a cool concrete-grey ground; the ink is near-black. Each exchange is set like a page of sides: the Interviewer's cue in large bold type, your line beneath it in comfortable reading type, and the Coach's notes pencilled in blue directly under your line, on a pencil-wash panel behind a dashed rule. This replaces the chat-bubble transcript (avatars, tinted \"me\" bubbles) the category defaults to.\n\nColour is scarce and assigned by meaning. Highlighter yellow marks where you are and what to look at (the current scene, the overall score, a run in progress, a selected option); director's-pencil blue is the Coach's voice and the interactive accent (links, focus, the coach input); green, amber and red appear only as real score states. Everything else is ink on paper. Density is calm: a single reading column with generous line height, one page per screen, no decoration layered on top.\n\nOne family, Atkinson Hyperlegible Next, carries everything, from the 88px score numeral to the 12px tracked speaker names, with tabular figures throughout. Depth comes from paper on ground and hairline rules, never from shadow.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Black-box studio band over a concrete ground; white script pages with hairline borders.",
      "Speaker names in tracked uppercase, set like character names in a script.",
      "Coach notes in pencil blue, under the line they are about, on a pencil-wash panel behind a 1px dashed pencil rule, at reading width (42em).",
      "Highlighter yellow always sits behind ink-coloured text, never used as text.",
      "Ink pill buttons; 6px page corners; flat surfaces.",
      "Light and dark schemes are both first-class and mapped role for role."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Highlighter Rule",
        "body": "Yellow is a mark laid behind ink-coloured text (`highlighter-ink`); it is never a text colour, and it marks one thing per region: where you are or what matters most.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Pencil Rule",
        "body": "Blue means the Coach or an affordance you can act on. Interviewer and candidate text are always ink.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Spike Tape Rule",
        "body": "Green, amber and red mark real states only, and a state colour always travels with an icon and a label, never alone.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Character Name Rule",
        "body": "Tracked uppercase is reserved for naming who speaks: Interviewer, You, Coach, and their qualifiers (Question n, Attempt n, to the coach). It is not a section label for arbitrary content.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Family Rule",
        "body": "Atkinson Hyperlegible Next everywhere; contrast comes from weight (400 to 800) and size, with negative tracking only at 1.5rem and above.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Paper Lift Rule",
        "body": "A surface separates from the ground by tone and a hairline border, never by a drop shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do set every exchange as speaker name, then text: muted Interviewer cue at `cue`, ink You line at `line`, pencil Coach note at `note` on the panel under the line.",
      "Do keep highlighter behind `highlighter-ink` text and keep it to one mark per region.",
      "Do separate surfaces with paper-on-concrete and a 1px `rule` hairline.",
      "Do make every button a pill, ink-filled for the main action and outlined in currentColor for the rest.",
      "Do pair every spike-tape state colour with an icon and a label.",
      "Do honour `prefers-reduced-motion` on every animation, as the sweep and the caret do.",
      "Do define every new colour in both schemes, role for role."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't render the transcript as chat bubbles with avatars or tinted \"me\" bubbles.",
      "Don't use drop shadows on papers, cards or buttons.",
      "Don't set text in highlighter yellow, or use pencil blue for anything the Interviewer or candidate says.",
      "Don't use tracked uppercase for anything other than naming who speaks.",
      "Don't introduce a second typeface or turn off tabular figures.",
      "Don't use green, amber or red decoratively."
    ]
  }
}
